      "role": "hook",
      "headline": "Milestone: halfway to Mastery. From a hand on a wall to three raised swords.",
      "body": "You started with a hand stencil on a cave wall. You've reached a painting of Roman brothers swearing an oath. Time to see how those pieces fit, and who was paying for the art along the way."
    },
    {
      "id": "card.art_history.050.c2",
      "type": "fact",
      "fact": "This whole chapter fits in the last ten minutes of the day.",
      "context": "Remember Level 1's clock, squeezing art's 67,800 years into 24 hours? Caravaggio's beam of light, about 1600, lands about 9 minutes before midnight. David's Oath, 1784, lands about 5 minutes before. Everything in this chapter happens in roughly four minutes of the day."
    },
